# Independent authoring review: WebKit synchronization

Reviewed the actual three Markdown deltas, actual Doc manuscript deltas and authoring/AGENTS guidance directly, independently of the author's check implementation. The author manifest SHA a7579cbeb29a0eb46731cb81da90d85079bda40e385ef44dd20a9d8b3c89e39e and every payload length/hash were checked. Old originals/drafts equal b29a420 Git blobs; new originals/drafts equal the actual files captured. Source-base means old canonical input and source-before.txt means the newly edited canonical input in the author's naming; these were not silently interchanged.

No blocking content/authoring issue found. The 05 change replaces exactly two grid-only sentences by four precise sentences: typed spans keep base/reading/notes separate, supported grid versus spec20 fallback, unchanged semantic HTML, and optional ruby/rt in another backend. The existing final CSS sentence and all other content are unchanged.

The 20 change removes the grid-only wording in one existing sentence and appends two paragraphs of five and four sentences. Ruby's last line and Anno's first line, source order/content preservation, no extra HTML table elements or JavaScript, WebKit motivation and unchanged typed semantics are all retained. The second paragraph preserves both exact official CSS2 link URLs/labels, behavioral testing rather than property support alone, scriptless documents and the explicit Wasm/Playground/assistive-technology limitation. One InlineCode uses a prefix Sentence and the link-bearing sentence uses prefix Link constructors; ordinary new sentences use literals.

The development change narrows the previously broad browser-unimplemented statement to browser Wasm/Playground, then adds five static-layout sentences, the exact shell RawCode including final LF, and two environment instructions. All numbers (13, 2, 3, 3), exact test filter/flags, pinned requirements path, three engine names, system-dependency command, failure/quality behavior and PowerShell UTF-8 qualification match the current source. The command-bearing environment sentence is explicit InlineCode; other sentences remain literals. No command is presented as a completed canonical migration.

The independent structural checker found 4 / 10 / 9 changed or added atoms across the three documents: 22 sentences and one RawCode. It compares changed sentence base text including punctuation/spaces against the source, exact RawCode bytes, two InlineCode values and two external link targets; unchanged atoms and unchanged line-byte spans are retained. The changed text has 134 Ruby occurrences, 98 distinct base/readings, checked for Kanji-only bases, unannotated ordinary Kanji and contextual readings. Source/draft diffs were also read in full so semantic limits, paragraph placement and changes outside the measured atoms are not inferred solely from extraction. No new translation is introduced, so no gratuitous Anno is required.

This review covers only the synchronized deltas. It does not rerun the prior full-page content review or claim new production parse/lower/HTML, human approval, canonical cutover or formal acceptance. The separate runtime/browser record addresses production layout checks.
